the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:

*a message* implies *a set*.
*a set* contains *an item*. 
*a message* is verifiable as true by *a user*. 
*a message* makes sense as a whole.
*a user* can decompose *a message* into *a set*.
there are enough references from scientific publications for every important statement in *a set*.
*a user* applies every specialized criterion on the subject matter of *a message* to validate *a set*.
there is no evidence to contradict *a set*. 

the knowledge base includes:

a message is verifiable as true by a user if
        the message makes sense as a whole
    and a user can decompose the message into a set
    and there are enough references from scientific publications for every important statement in the set
    and the user applies every specialized criterion on the subject matter of the message to validate the set
    and there is no evidence to contradict the set. 

scenario chemical risk is:
    message 1 is 'Compound X is an organic ester and it is FDA-approved for human consumption'.
    message 1 makes sense as a whole.
    % [Decomposition:] The system breaks the message
    smart person can decompose message 1 into set A.
    message 1 implies set A.
    set A contains 'Compound X is an organic ester.'.
    set A contains 'Compound X is FDA-approved for human consumption.'.
    % [Scientific Backing:] The system queries a verified database (e.g., PubChem). It finds the first is true but the second has no corresponding entry.
    % [Non-Falsification:] The system finds a recent 2024 study indicating Compound X is toxic to gut flora.
    one expects [].

scenario chemical safety is:
    message 1 is 'Compound X is an organic ester and it is FDA-approved for human consumption'.
    message 1 makes sense as a whole.
    % [Decomposition:] The system breaks the message
    lucky person can decompose message 1 into set A.
    message 1 implies set A.
    set A contains 'Compound X is an organic ester.'.
    set A contains 'Compound X is FDA-approved for human consumption.'.
    % [Scientific Backing:] The system queries a verified database (e.g., PubChem). It finds support for all items in the set.
    there are enough references from scientific publications for every important statement in set A.
    lucky person applies every specialized criterion on the subject matter of message 1 to validate set A.
    % [Non-Falsification:] After checking the evidence, there is no evidence the refute the items in the set
    there is no evidence to contradict set A.
    one expects ["message 1 is verifiable as true by lucky person"].

query one is:
    which message is verifiable as true by which user. 